WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:26.820
So during that absolutely stunning interview
with Fox News's Chris Wallace, which we looked

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:33.540
at earlier, Chris Wallace mentions a Fox News
poll where Biden is ahead of Trump 49 to 41.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.559
And the poll actually has a ton of fascinating
data points now as a reminder.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:40.590
Fox News polling and Fox News Channel are
two different things.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:45.060
Fox News polling is actually considered quite
good and and accurate.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.879
So a few things as we get into it.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.780
This is a poll of registered voters.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.800
Remember that the least accurate in terms
of predicting an election is to just survey

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.499
all adults.

00:00:56.499 --> 00:01:01.390
More accurate is registered voters and then
ideal is likely voters, although you tend

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:05.030
to see fewer likely voter polls this early.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.170
You see more of those as we get closer to
Election Day.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.330
Now, one other thing just to short circuit
those claims about, oh, they only called landlines.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.250
We can't trust this, as you can see in the
methodology.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:22.569
This was done with a 237 landline recipients
and eight hundred and sixty seven cell phones.

00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:24.200
So they call cell phones.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.710
This was mostly cell phones.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:32.690
Now, on key issues, super important on the
economy, 47 to 47.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.539
Biden and Trump on.

00:01:34.539 --> 00:01:36.850
Who is better to handle the economy?

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.899
The economy has been Trump's one issue lately
where he was polling better than Joe Biden

00:01:41.899 --> 00:01:43.470
last week in the Quinnipiac poll.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:47.310
Joe Biden pulled better than Trump on the
economy in this Fox News poll.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.310
They are tied.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.060
That's not good for Trump.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.490
Not surprisingly, on race relations, Trump
is way underwater.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.890
Only 35 approve.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.440
Thirty five percent approve of Trump.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.209
On race relations, 56 percent disapprove.

00:01:59.209 --> 00:02:06.770
I already mentioned Biden up 49 to 41 by eight
in the general election poll right now.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.599
Four percent say they would vote for other.

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:12.080
Five percent say they don't know yet.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:17.590
And then now it gets really interesting when
vote when a poll recip a poll, a poll.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.590
What would we call them?

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.590
Poll takers.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.860
Subjects were asked about vote by mail.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.680
Sixty three percent of the country says they
favor vote by mail, compared to 28 percent

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.110
who oppose.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:34.880
This suggests that Trump, loudly opposing
vote by mail, as he has been doing, may not

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.420
really be a good strategy to bring more people
over to his side.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.440
Now, this is really important and very interesting.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:48.980
I recently said if they have debates, Biden
shouldn't go at Trump's insults or wacky behavior.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.209
I said there are three primary issues that
have hurt Trump and that should be the focus

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:59.110
corona virus, the economy as a result of corona
virus and the protests.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.490
Jorge Floyd, race issues.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:06.510
When asked what are the most important issues
today, the issues are.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.000
Twenty nine percent say coronavirus.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.780
Fifteen percent say the economy, jobs and
unemployment.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.450
And 10 percent say race relations and police
issues.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:21.420
So those three issues are the top issues for
54 percent of the country.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.030
It's really important to confirm our hypotheses.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:30.660
It appeared that Corona virus, the economy
and race relations were the most important

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.340
issues and the ones that had hurt Trump the
most.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.950
And indeed, it appears that that is the case.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.780
Now, last thing, there was a question about
mental soundness.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.000
For years we've been seeing concerning signs
from Trump about his cognitive state.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.080
There's also a Joe Biden has dementia movement.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:50.930
I've admitted Biden has definitely slowed
down from where he was in his 60s, despite

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.490
it not appearing to be dementia.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:56.020
According to every mental health expert I've
spoken to, the poll asked.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:01.580
Do you think Biden and Trump have the mental
soundness to serve effectively as president?

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:05.050
Forty seven percent believe Biden has the
mental soundness.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.060
Only 43 percent believe Trump does.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.890
Now, those numbers are just really low.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.530
The fact that neither candidate has half the
country believing they are mentally sound

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.819
is a problem.

00:04:14.819 --> 00:04:18.750
But note that 14 percent aren't sure about
Biden.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.220
Seven percent aren't sure about Trump.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:28.150
The important takeaway is more people question
Trump's fitness for office than Biden's, although

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.180
not by a huge margin.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:34.740
So the big takeaways here are our instincts
about what matters.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.000
This election has been right.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:43.990
The polls are consistently showing similar
results and we all have to assume nothing

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:50.360
and vote like our state depends on our vote
to choose between Trump and Biden.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:57.460
That's how we should imagine we are going
to act on a on November 3rd or before if you're

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.460
voting early.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.630
And I hope many of you do.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:03.590
My vote could swing my state from Trump to
Biden.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:06.230
I'm sure as hell voting in that case.

